> [!NOTE]
> This bug was discovered by Codex GPT-6.2 Astra in the course of working on another task. I, @rgov, reviewed its work and authorized it to file this issue. I edited this report for clarity.

## Description

Humble’s zstd file-compression plugin leaves an incomplete frame when the input file size is an exact multiple of its 128 KiB read buffer, even though it returns success. This can result in completed SQLite bag segments that `zstd -d` rejects with `premature end`.

`zstd` will still decompress the full file, but to silence the error one can append an empty block to the file: 

```
printf '\001\000\000' >> repaired.db3.zstd
```

### Expected Behavior

Every compressed file decompresses to the original bytes, including files that end exactly on a buffer boundary.

### Actual Behavior

Files which are multiples of 128 KiB cannot be decompressed.

```text
131071 bytes: PASS
131072 bytes: FAIL (Src size is incorrect)
131073 bytes: PASS
1048576 bytes: FAIL (Src size is incorrect)
```

## Diagnosis

`input.eof()` remains false when a read of the final 128 KiB bytes fills the buffer exactly. Hence the compressor uses `ZSTD_e_continue`.

The next read returns zero bytes and sets EOF. The `size > 0` guard then skips the call that would pass `ZSTD_e_end`, and the loop exits with the frame unfinished.

https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/blob/bc63926c2e06efa480a957549be88b614fa96c82/rosbag2_compression_zstd/src/rosbag2_compression_zstd/zstd_compressor.cpp#L76-L94

Changing the guard to `if (size > 0 || input.eof())` allowed the final zero-byte read to finish the frame. All four inputs then decompressed byte-for-byte.


## To Reproduce

Save the script below as `reproduce-rosbag2-zstd.sh` and run it in the official Humble image. The script exits 1 if any file fails to round-trip.

```sh
docker run --rm -i --network none ros:humble-ros-base bash -s < reproduce-rosbag2-zstd.sh
```

<details>
<summary>reproduce-rosbag2-zstd.sh</summary>

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Run in the official image: docker run --rm -i --network none ros:humble-ros-base bash -s < reproduce-rosbag2-zstd.sh
# Exit 0 if every input round-trips, 1 on a failed round-trip.
set -eo pipefail
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
dpkg-query -W ros-humble-rosbag2-compression-zstd libzstd1

workdir=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf -- "$workdir"' EXIT
cd "$workdir"

cat > CMakeLists.txt <<'CMAKE'
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16)
project(reproduce LANGUAGES CXX)
find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)
find_package(rosbag2_compression_zstd REQUIRED)
add_executable(reproduce reproduce.cpp)
ament_target_dependencies(reproduce rosbag2_compression_zstd)
target_link_libraries(reproduce zstd)
CMAKE

cat > reproduce.cpp <<'CPP'
#include <rosbag2_compression_zstd/zstd_compressor.hpp>
#include <zstd.h>

#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
#include <iterator>
#include <string>

int main()
{
  const auto block = ZSTD_CStreamInSize();
  bool passed = true;

  for (auto size : {block - 1, block, block + 1, 8 * block}) {
    rosbag2_compression_zstd::ZstdCompressor compressor;
    const std::string input(size, 'a');
    const auto path = std::to_string(size);
    std::ofstream(path, std::ios::binary).write(input.data(), size);

    std::ifstream file(compressor.compress_uri(path), std::ios::binary);
    const std::string frame{std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(file), {}};
    std::string output(size, '\0');
    const auto result = ZSTD_decompress(&output[0], size, frame.data(), frame.size());

    std::cout << size << " bytes: ";
    if (ZSTD_isError(result)) {
      std::cout << "FAIL (" << ZSTD_getErrorName(result) << ")\n";
      passed = false;
    } else if (result != size || output != input) {
      std::cout << "FAIL (decoded content differs)\n";
      passed = false;
    } else {
      std::cout << "PASS\n";
    }
  }
  return passed ? 0 : 1;
}
CPP

cmake -S . -B build >/dev/null
cmake --build build >/dev/null
./build/reproduce
```

</details>

## System

- OS: Ubuntu 22.04 (Jammy), arm64
- ROS 2 Distro: Humble
- Install Method: APT binaries in the official `ros:humble-ros-base` image
- Version: `ros-humble-rosbag2-compression-zstd 0.15.17-1jammy.20261106.225903`, `libzstd1 1.4.8+dfsg-3build1`
- Image digest: `ros@sha256:a18afd4a42ad603579d03b9012385dfeaf2e848423f0a6c41699766e7849c86c`

## Additional context

Two earlier reports describe similar premature-end errors. The original input sizes are unknown, so the cause of those particular failures is unconfirmed. [rosbag2#1348](https://github.com/ros2/rosbag2/issues/1348), [ros2#1476](https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1476).
